{"id": "R-consolidation-input", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Consolidation gives the model no file tools: crank-mem selects cited files, admits each only if it is inside the project by real path, not sensitive by either name in any case, not hidden, regular and within size, and sends redacted, line-numbered excerpts marked as data. Uncited proposals are not accepted.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}, {"rel": "depends_on", "to": "AS-license@1"}]}
{"id": "R-consolidation-switch", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Consolidation has its own switch, off by default; turning digests on does not turn consolidation on.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-index-containment", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Nothing outside the project by real path is indexed or read: every index and read path passes one shared gate (real-path containment, sensitivity on requested and resolved names, regular file).", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-monorepo-git", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "code", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "A project rooted in a repository subdirectory honours the enclosing repository: its listing respects .gitignore, exclude mode writes to the enclosing repository's exclude file, and a git failure inside a repository keeps the previous index rather than walking unfiltered.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "R-installer", "version": 1, "type": "requirement", "subject": "design", "epistemic": "provisional", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "A guided one-command install: small core by default (dashboard and model optional), Claude/Codex/both selection, preview of every config change, resumable or reversible after interruption, safe repeat, upgrade and uninstall, consolidation off and Codex trust review on by default.", "relations": [{"rel": "serves", "to": "P0@2"}]}
{"id": "D-consolidation-optionA", "version": 1, "type": "decision", "subject": "design", "status": "accepted", "decided_by": "AU-owner", "authored_by": "claude:abi", "text": "Adopt the excerpt-only consolidation design (Option A in PROPOSAL.md) for this copy.", "source": "Zach 2026-11-10: \"Sounds good to me!\" after the excerpt-only explanation", "relations": [{"rel": "depends_on", "to": "R-consolidation-input@1"}]}
